Z||000006||88 Database Nut||09-25-2001||10:21 PM||||Thanks Guys! The yard let us have it for a few hundred.  Really just a token fee.  The yard manager admitted he had less in it than that, but I wasn't about to argue.  After all, they aren't in the business of giving stuff away, and they very, very easily could have put the kabosh on the deal many times, to make it easier on themselves.  They helped me put my wheels on it, and set it up<BR>in the front so my flatbed driver could easily pick it up.  I'm their number one fan right now, I'll tell you that!  I guess it was just my turn to get lucky.  Either that, or this car has about 9 lives (well, 8 now).<P>Goodnight to everyone in Fieroland, where all the roads and ladies are curvy and fun... (where did that come from?  Why, the RunForThe Hills6 event of this weekend, of course!  Way to go David Hunter of the Alabama Fieros, this was the best I've been to and one hell of a blast, even if I slept through the doorprize drawing)<P><BR>||||reg||1
